------------------------------------------------------------
Node ID=1 campfire
Text=<Cold ash, and five bedrolls, each slept in once. They camped here the night before they went in.>
Should Have Voiceover=0
------------------------------------------------------------
Node ID=1 campfire alt
Text=<Cold ash, and five bedrolls, each slept in once. The ash is two days old, no more. Boot prints lead to the gate. None come back.>
Should Have Voiceover=0
------------------------------------------------------------
Node ID=2 dead snakebreed
Text=<One of the creatures, cut nearly in half by a single stroke. The first thing that came out of the treeline, and the last thing this knight did.>
Should Have Voiceover=0
------------------------------------------------------------
Node ID=3 barricade
Text=<A barricade, built to hold the door and broken from the inside. They opened it to sally out, and died in the doorway.>
Should Have Voiceover=0
------------------------------------------------------------
Node ID=4 jailor
Text=<A jailor of the abbey's own cells, in the Inquisition's black. His ring of keys is gone.>
Should Have Voiceover=0
------------------------------------------------------------
Node ID=4 jailor alt
Text=<A jailor of the abbey's own cells, in the Inquisition's black. The keys were cut from his belt, not taken from his hand. Someone wanted the cells opened, not locked.>
Should Have Voiceover=0
------------------------------------------------------------
Node ID=5 candles
Text=<The candles are lit. The wax has barely run.>
Should Have Voiceover=0
------------------------------------------------------------
Node ID=5 candles alt
Text=<The candles are lit, and the wax has barely run. Lit within the hour. Someone is still tending them.>
Should Have Voiceover=0
------------------------------------------------------------
Node ID=6 druid gate
Text=<The gate is older than anything the abbey built over it. The carvings are not Christian. Nobody thought to remove them.>
Should Have Voiceover=0
------------------------------------------------------------
Node ID=6 druid gate alt
Text=<Oak leaf and sickle, cut before Rome came: the marks of the druids of Gaul. The monks raised their sanctuary on a council-ground and kept its door.>
Should Have Voiceover=0
------------------------------------------------------------
Node ID=7 altar
Text=<The altar. The reliquary that stood on it is gone; the velvet cloth still holds the shape of what rested there for three hundred years.>
Should Have Voiceover=0
------------------------------------------------------------
Node ID=8 no monks
Text=<Knights of the Temple, men of the Inquisition, the abbey's own jailors. Not one monk among them. The cells below are empty.>
Should Have Voiceover=0
------------------------------------------------------------
Node ID=6 druid gate sylvant
Text=<The gate is older than anything the abbey built over it. The carvings are not Christian, and you did not need to be told: your blood knew them before your eyes did.>
Should Have Voiceover=0
------------------------------------------------------------
Node ID=6 druid gate wielder
Text=<The gate is older than anything the abbey built over it. The carvings are not Christian. Put a hand to them and the spirit in you answers - faintly, the way it answers the Ways crystals. Someone here worked the same magic, long before there were Wielders.>
Should Have Voiceover=0
------------------------------------------------------------
Node ID=9 inquisitor
Text=<A man of the Inquisition, his seal still on his belt. He died with his back to the cells.>
Should Have Voiceover=0
------------------------------------------------------------
Node ID=9 sealed order
Text=<A man of the Inquisition, his seal still on his belt. Inside his coat, an order under Raphael's mark: hold the cells until relieved; let no one speak with the prisoners. You are of the Inquisition. Nobody told you the abbey kept prisoners.>
Should Have Voiceover=0
